,"borrowedGeometryFrom":null,"enemyDetails":{"norport_civilian":{"slug":"norport_civilian","name":"Norport Civilian","icon":"/enemies-icons/Norport Civilian.webp","rank":"Normal","race":null,"movement":"Ground","attackPosition":null,"damageType":["No Damage"],"flavourText":"Ordinary folk scattered throughout Norport Borough. Abandoned by Londinium and subjected to the Sarkaz's high-handed blockade, these orphans have become the ones most deeply affected by the haze of war.","abilities":["Friendly Unit","Once their identity is confirmed, restores your max DP after retreating to the Objective Point"],"levelCount":1,"level":0,"levelAssumed":false,"statsOverridden":false,"moveSpeed":0.65,"stats":{"hp":5000,"atk":250,"def":50,"res":0,"elementalRes":null,"elementalDamageRes":null,"attackInterval":2.5}},"pathfinder_spymaster":{"slug":"pathfinder_spymaster","name":"Pathfinder Spymaster","icon":"/enemies-icons/Pathfinder Spymaster.webp","rank":"Normal","race":null,"movement":"Ground","attackPosition":"Melee","damageType":["Physical"],"flavourText":"A spy hired by a mysterious employer to monitor their rivals while disguised as civilians. These seasoned operatives will occasionally employ less orthodox methods to get their more impatient rivals to let down their guard.","abilities":["Spy","When their identity is revealed, the next attack's ATK is greatly increased"],"levelCount":1,"level":0,"levelAssumed":false,"statsOverridden":false,"moveSpeed":0.65,"stats":{"hp":8000,"atk":600,"def":350,"res":20,"elementalRes":null,"elementalDamageRes":null,"attackInterval":2.3}},"rebellion_agitator":{"slug":"rebellion_agitator","name":"Rebellion Agitator","icon":"/enemies-icons/Rebellion Agitator.webp","rank":"Elite","race":null,"movement":"Ground","attackPosition":"Melee","damageType":["Arts"],"flavourText":"Disruptors that constantly bypass the blockade. They weaken the enemy's forces from within by taking the initiative to whip the masses into a frenzy, who in turn break down the borough defenses all on their own.","abilities":["When not blocked, all unrevealed Civilians or Spies cannot be blocked"],"levelCount":1,"level":0,"levelAssumed":false,"statsOverridden":false,"moveSpeed":0.6,"stats":{"hp":12000,"atk":300,"def":150,"res":50,"elementalRes":null,"elementalDamageRes":null,"attackInterval":5}},"sarkaz_greatswordsman_leader":{"slug":"sarkaz_greatswordsman_leader","name":"Sarkaz Greatswordsman Leader","icon":"/enemies-icons/Sarkaz Greatswordsman Leader.webp","rank":"Elite","race":"Sarkaz","movement":"Ground","attackPosition":"Melee","damageType":["Physical"],"flavourText":"A mercenary from Sarkaz, more dangerous than a normal Sarkaz Swordsman. The Originium inside them has boosted their physical abilities, allowing them to wield larger weapons with ease and withstand more damage.","abilities":[],"levelCount":1,"level":0,"levelAssumed":false,"statsOverridden":false,"moveSpeed":0.85,"stats":{"hp":15000,"atk":750,"def":250,"res":50,"elementalRes":null,"elementalDamageRes":null,"attackInterval":2}},"sarkaz_absurdist_tyrant_captain":{"slug":"sarkaz_absurdist_tyrant_captain","name":"Sarkaz Absurdist Tyrant Captain","icon":"/enemies-icons/Sarkaz Absurdist Tyrant Captain.webp","rank":"Elite","race":"Sarkaz","movement":"Ground","attackPosition":"Melee","damageType":["Physical"],"flavourText":"A product of the cooperation between the Damazti Cluster and the Military Commission, able to change their appearance with Arts. They can skillfully manipulate their flesh without damaging their brains, and are used to employing their intimidating forms to gain an advantage in battle.","abilities":["Can only be blocked by Operators with 3 or more Block","First attack deals Splash damage"],"levelCount":1,"level":0,"levelAssumed":false,"statsOverridden":false,"moveSpeed":0.8,"stats":{"hp":25000,"atk":1200,"def":800,"res":20,"elementalRes":null,"elementalDamageRes":null,"attackInterval":2.9}},"shadowing_trilby_asher":{"slug":"shadowing_trilby_asher","name":"'Shadowing Trilby Asher'","icon":"/enemies-icons/'Shadowing Trilby Asher'.webp","rank":"Elite","race":null,"movement":"Ground","attackPosition":"Melee","damageType":["Physical"],"flavourText":"To the Duke of Caster, a 'Trilby Asher' is more of a consumable than a collectible. On the day a 'Trilby Asher' is honored with the job, another 'Shadowing Trilby Asher' is also born—only succeeding their predecessor when their mentor dies.","abilities":["After several attacks, moves towards the next checkpoint for the next attack"],"levelCount":1,"level":0,"levelAssumed":false,"statsOverridden":false,"moveSpeed":0.7,"stats":{"hp":15000,"atk":1800,"def":375,"res":30,"elementalRes":null,"elementalDamageRes":null,"attackInterval":6}},"damazti_cluster_enemy_1542_wdslm":{"slug":"damazti_cluster_enemy_1542_wdslm","name":"'Damazti Cluster'","icon":"/enemies-icons/'Damazti Cluster'.webp","rank":"Boss","race":null,"movement":"Ground","attackPosition":"Melee","damageType":["Physical"],"flavourText":"A long-lived that has drifted away from the Sarkaz Royal Court. They have taken the rise and fall of the various races as a sort of life experience, but the Damazti Cluster has yet to find the answer to what 'living' means.","abilities":["Spy","Whenever a certain percentage of HP is lost, summons an Isomorphic Fragment on an Operator or on the field that shares HP with self;","Both the Damazti Cluster and Isomorphic Fragments take reduced Physical and Arts damage for every Isomorphic Fragment present on the field","Both the Damazti Cluster and Isomorphic Fragments are Invulnerable while their identities have yet to be revealed","Attacks inflict Corrosion","First Form","Periodically releases [Derivative Iteration]: both the Damazti Cluster and Isomorphic Fragments simultaneously deal Physical damage to a target","When defeated for the first time, deals continuous Arts damage to all units around Damazti Cluster or Isomorphic Fragments while regenerating itself","Second Form","Periodically releases [Lif